{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 28,
      "name": "Moon Jump",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "Each variant is a small set of islands tuned to one gravity value. The fun is in hand-placed arcs (over walls, round pillars, under ceilings), and a generator would make them samey or unfair. About 16 clean versions cover the idea.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "ghost see-through zone parts (wind, gust) the client checks the local player against",
          "lift / bounce: the client already pushes the local character inside a zone",
          "slide motion (bobbing hazard blobs, drifting islands) and flip timing (on/off with period and duty)",
          "red goo hazard look and the fall-back-to-start rule",
          "spec helper launchReaches that checks reach from a launch speed and gravity",
          "hazard touch = back to the start pad, once built for Crusher Alley (idea 1)"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "'moon' zone kind, a sister of Updraft's lift zone (idea 5): same client check of the local root against the zone, but instead of pushing up, a VectorForce carries (1 - gravity) of your weight while inside; removed on leaving. Client only.",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "bubble dome look (big see-through sphere, sparkles, moon sign; deeper tint = lower gravity) and a jump sparkle trail",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "spec: moon gaps and rises go through the one shared launch reach check (Bounce Chain's launchReaches, idea 4, also used by Ice Slide 6 and Speed Strip 16) with that zone's gravity and 80% spare; the 6-stud GAP_MAX and 3.5 RISE_MAX only apply outside bubbles",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Moon Pulse: the zone's on/off hangs on Beat Pads' BeatClock (idea 18) for its glow and tick, not a timer of its own",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "soft 'whoom' sound on entering and leaving a bubble so the gravity change is heard",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "A big pale bubble dome with drifting sparkles and a moon sign marks low gravity; the deeper its tint, the floatier it is. Entering plays a soft whoom and your jumps leave a sparkle trail; leaving plays the whoom backwards. Moon jumps start from your own jump, never from a pad or a wind column, so they read apart from Bounce Chain and Updraft.",
      "generator": null,
